Current Version can be found [[Ice Replica|here]].
Ice Replica was released in '''Beta 27.0''' as Patience's 3rd Rare spell. '''Beta 32.0''' dropped its cost from 2G to 1G. '''Beta 39.0''' returned its cost to 2G but also reworked its effect. Before, it would exactly copy a paralyzed non-DT monster to your deck. If this was used on an ally monster, it would always go to the top of your deck. Now, it will add an [[Ice Cap]], [[Ice]] and [[Snowman]] to your hand (always in that order, even if the card mentioned Ice before Ice Cap). '''Beta 42.0''' increased its cost to 3G.

With the class rework of '''Beta 55.0''', Ice Replica's design was mostly moved to [[Cold Winter]], while Ice Replica itself regained some of its old design. Now, still for 3G, it can Paralyze any non-DT monster on the board. After doing so, when your turn ends, a copy of that monster will be added to your hand. If it was an ally monster, the copy will have its cost reduced by 2G. 
'''Beta 61.0''' dropped its cost from 3G to 2G.
